CORE
main.c
--mmio-region 0x1000:256:strong _ --no-pointer-check --no-bounds-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
value read back from the region: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
A strongly-ordered MMIO region (the default type) is modelled precisely by its
backing array, so a value written to the region reads back exactly. Compare
weak.desc.
